	<item>
		<title>By: Haqiqa Nuri</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=720&#038;cpage=1#comment-6388</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Haqiqa Nuri]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 10 Oct 2010 22:03:49 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=720#comment-6388</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[A memory of Jamshed which stays with me, was the feeling at the end of a dance at Breitenbush which he led. There were only eight of us, years ago, dancing in a small dome or yurt. He led us to such a lovely state, that it stands out in memory as the best dance event I ever attended, even compared to all the large camps with hundreds of us.
          Insh&#039;allah he&#039;s in that state now! Happy travels in the heart of the Beloved, Jamshed, thanks for your presence, and Ya Salaam!
With love and gratitude, Haqiqa Nuri]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>A memory of Jamshed which stays with me, was the feeling at the end of a dance at Breitenbush which he led. There were only eight of us, years ago, dancing in a small dome or yurt. He led us to such a lovely state, that it stands out in memory as the best dance event I ever attended, even compared to all the large camps with hundreds of us.<br />
          Insh&#8217;allah he&#8217;s in that state now! Happy travels in the heart of the Beloved, Jamshed, thanks for your presence, and Ya Salaam!<br />
With love and gratitude, Haqiqa Nuri</p>
]]></content:encoded>
